#HELPS

0 AID~
Syntax: cast aid <character>

Calls a god's aid on somebody: hitroll rises by a tenth of your level and
maximum hit points by 20 plus up to half your level, for 7 plus a quarter
of your level in ticks.  It cannot be laid twice.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:15  Cleric:13  Thief:18  Warrior:20  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLESS, CURE CRITICAL, BENEDICTIONS
~

0 'ACID BLAST' 'COLOUR SPRAY' 'COLOR SPRAY' 'MAGIC MISSILE' 'SHOCK SPHERE'~
Syntax: cast 'acid blast'    <victim>
        cast 'colour spray'  <victim>
        cast 'magic missile' <victim>
        cast 'shock sphere'  <victim>

Single-target attack spells; the higher-level ones hurt more.  A saving
throw halves all but shock sphere.

  ACID BLAST     acid, many dice per caster level.  Full mages, from 28.
  COLOUR SPRAY   light; a victim who fails the save may be blinded (a
                 player only by a caster more than five levels above).
  MAGIC MISSILE  one missile, plus one every ten levels, each saved
                 against apart.
  SHOCK SPHERE   lightning no save reduces.  Necromancers, from 15.

Spell it COLOUR: CAST 'COLOUR SPRAY' BOB or CAST COLOUR BOB.  The spelling
COLOR finds no spell; CAST suggests the right one.

For colour spray, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:16  Cleric:18  Thief:20  Warrior:22  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For magic missile, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:1  Cleric:3  Thief:4  Warrior:5  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FIRE SPELLS, COLD SPELLS, ELECTRIC SPELLS, HARMFUL
~

0 'GHOSTLY PRESENCE'~
Syntax: cast 'ghostly presence'

Turns you into a ghost for a while: you cannot be attacked, and you
cannot attack.  Necromancers only, from level 25.

See also: ANIMATE PARTS, LIFE-UNDEATH, PASS DOOR
~

0 'ANIMATE PARTS'~
Syntax: cast 'animate parts'

Hurls something dead at whoever you are fighting; you must be fighting.
A body part lying in the room (BUTCHER makes them) is thrown first and
hurts most: a heart, then an arm or leg, then guts, then a head.  With
none to hand you throw carrion from the air, which always works and
hurts least.  Necromancers only, from level 5.

See also: BUTCHER, EMBALM, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 ARMOR SHIELD 'STONE SKIN' SHROUD 'MAJOR GLOBE'~
Syntax: cast armor <character>
        cast shield <character>
        cast 'stone skin'
        cast shroud
        cast 'major globe'

Protective spells that improve armour class:

  ARMOR        20 points; may be cast on others
  SHIELD       20 points; may be cast on others
  STONE SKIN   40 points; never takes on a monk or necromancer, potions
               included
  SHROUD       35 points; necromancers only, from level 26
  MAJOR GLOBE  80 points; cannot be combined with any of the others

For armor, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:3  Cleric:3  Thief:8  Warrior:7  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:3

For shield, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:20  Cleric:24  Thief:25  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:23

For stone skin, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:25  Cleric:29  Thief:27  Warrior:30  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For major globe, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:30  Cleric:30  Thief:35  Warrior:40  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:32

See also: PROTECTION EVIL, ENCHANT ARMOR, PROTECTIVE
~
0 'BEWITCH WEAPON' BEWITCH~
Syntax: cast 'bewitch weapon' <weapon>

Curses a weapon you carry so it cannot be removed once wielded, and no
disarm will budge it.  It always works on a weapon no higher in level
than you; one already bewitched is refused.  REMOVE CURSE lifts it.

  - Costs 65 mana.  Necromancers only, from level 25.

See also: CURSE, DISARM, REMOVE CURSE
~

0 BLESS~
Syntax: cast bless <character>

Improves hitroll and saving throw against spells, by an amount that
grows with the caster's level.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:9  Cleric:6  Thief:12  Warrior:11  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CURSE, KNOW ALIGNMENT, BENEDICTIONS
~

0 BLINDNESS~
Syntax: cast blindness <victim>

Blinds the victim for a time: they cannot see the room, its people or
things, and fight worse.  CURE BLINDNESS ends it.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:8  Thief:15  Warrior:13  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:15

See also: CURE BLINDNESS, DIRT KICKING
~

0 BUTCHER~
Syntax: cast butcher <corpse>

Cuts a corpse into five body parts for ANIMATE PARTS.  Necromancers only,
from level 10.

See also: ANIMATE PARTS, EMBALM, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 CALM~
Syntax: cast calm

Tries to stop every fight in the room.  The more fighters, and the higher
their levels, the harder it is; a failure says the fighting was too
fierce.  Undead and magic-immune mobiles, and anybody berserk, frenzied
or already calm, are passed over, and everybody else is calmed.
Fighters may attack again at once.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:22  Cleric:20  Thief:28  Warrior:30  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BENEDICTIONS, BLESS, FRENZY
~

0 'CAUSE LIGHT' 'CAUSE SERIOUS' 'CAUSE CRITICAL' HARM~
Syntax: cast 'cause light'    <victim>
        cast 'cause serious'  <victim>
        cast 'cause critical' <victim>
        cast harm             <victim>

Inflict wounds on one victim; the higher-level spells hurt more.

For cause light, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:4  Cleric:2  Thief:5  Warrior:3  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:4

For cause serious, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:8  Thief:11  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:18

For cause critical, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:18  Cleric:14  Thief:22  Warrior:19  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For harm, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:25  Cleric:24  Thief:32  Warrior:28  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CURE LIGHT, CURE CRITICAL, HARMFUL
~

62 'CHANGE SEX'~
Syntax: cast 'change sex' <victim>

Changes the victim's sex for about two ticks per caster level.  A saving
throw resists it, and it cannot be laid twice.  Staff only.

See also: BENEDICTIONS
~

0 'CHARM PERSON'~
Syntax: cast 'charm person' <victim>

Makes the victim follow you and obey ORDER for a few ticks.  You answer
for what your followers do.

  - Fails half the time, and always on a victim above your level, one
    already charmed, a mount or anything charm-proof.
  - The mayor forbids it inside a city's law rooms.
  - Hyrule's creatures cannot be charmed.
  - It is an attack: cast at a player outside the arena it makes you
    WANTED.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:20  Cleric:22  Thief:24  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: ORDER, FOLLOW, PKILL
~

0 'COLD SPELLS' 'CHILL TOUCH' 'CONE OF COLD' BLIZZARD ICICLE~
Syntax: cast 'chill touch'  <victim>
        cast 'cone of cold'
        cast blizzard
        cast icicle         <victim>

Cold damage spells.

  CHILL TOUCH   one victim; also lowers their strength
  CONE OF COLD  a cone that may strike several victims, each with a save
  BLIZZARD      everybody in the room you could attack; full mages, from
                level 37
  ICICLE        one victim

For chill touch, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:4  Cleric:5  Thief:6  Warrior:7  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:9

For cone of cold, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:32  Cleric:33  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:35

For icicle, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:24  Cleric:16  Thief:27  Warrior:27  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:21

See also: FIRE SPELLS, ELECTRIC SPELLS, ELEMENTAL
~

0 'CONTINUAL LIGHT'~
Syntax: cast 'continual light'

Creates a ball of light to hold as a light source.  It never runs out.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:5  Cleric:4  Thief:7  Warrior:6  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: INFRAVISION, LIGHT SPELLS, CREATION
~

0 'CONTROL WEATHER'~
Syntax: cast 'control weather' better
        cast 'control weather' worse

Makes the weather better or worse from the next tick.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:27  Cleric:28  Thief:32  Warrior:32  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: WEATHERSPELLS, CALL LIGHTNING
~

0 'CREATE FOOD'~
Syntax: cast 'create food'

Creates a magic mushroom that anybody can eat.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:5  Thief:12  Warrior:11  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CREATE WATER, CREATE SPRING, CREATION
~

0 'CREATE SPRING'~
Syntax: cast 'create spring'

Brings a magical spring out of the ground; drink from it like a fountain.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:16  Cleric:14  Thief:20  Warrior:18  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CREATE FOOD, CREATE WATER, CREATION
~

0 'CREATE SKELETON' 'CREATE WRAITH' 'CREATE VAMPIRE'~
Syntax: cast create skeleton [corpse]
        cast create wraith [corpse]
        cast create vampire [corpse]

Raises an undead servant that fights for you.  Necromancers only:
skeleton from level 15, wraith from 30, vampire from 45.

  - Name a corpse, or any NPC corpse in the room is used.  A servant
    raised from a body is half again as strong, lasts twice as long and
    keeps some of what the dead thing was worth.  With no corpse it
    comes thin.
  - Its strength follows your level, not the corpse's.
  - Your will bears 10: a skeleton takes 2, a wraith 5, a vampire 10.
  - Each servant lasts a set time, then departs.

See also: ANIMATE PARTS, BUTCHER, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 'CREATE WATER'~
Syntax: cast 'create water' <drink container>

Fills a drink container with water.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:3  Thief:11  Warrior:12  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CREATE FOOD, CREATE SPRING, CREATION
~

0 'CURE BLINDNESS'~
Syntax: cast 'cure blindness' <character>

Cures blindness.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:6  Thief:12  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: BLINDNESS, CURATIVE
~

0 'CURE LIGHT' 'CURE SERIOUS' 'CURE CRITICAL' HEALSPELL 'MASS HEALING'~
Syntax: cast 'cure light'    <character>
        cast 'cure serious'  <character>
        cast 'cure critical' <character>
        cast heal            <character>
        cast 'mass healing'

Restore hit points; the higher-level spells heal more.

  HEAL          100 hit points to level 25, two more a level above: 130
                at 40, 150 at 50, 168 at 59.  A non-cleric heals two
                thirds as much.
  MASS HEALING  heals and refreshes everybody in the room.  Full clerics,
                from level 38.

For cure light, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:2  Cleric:1  Thief:5  Warrior:3  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For cure serious, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:7  Thief:12  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For cure critical, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:14  Cleric:13  Thief:16  Warrior:15  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For heal, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:25  Cleric:23  Thief:32  Warrior:30  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: AID, CAUSE LIGHT, HEALING
~

0 'CURE DISEASE'~
Syntax: cast 'cure disease' <character>

Cures plague and other disease.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:15  Cleric:13  Thief:18  Warrior:16  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: PLAGUE, CURE POISON, CURATIVE
~

0 'CURE NIGHTMARE'~
Syntax: cast 'cure nightmare' <character>

Ends the psionic NIGHTMARE, so the victim regains hit points, mana and
movement again.  From level 20, for anybody who buys the CURATIVE group
(the clerics' guild).

See also: NIGHTMARE, CURATIVE
~

0 'CURE POISON'~
Syntax: cast 'cure poison' <character>

Cures poison.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:15  Cleric:14  Thief:17  Warrior:16  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: POISON, CURE DISEASE, CURATIVE
~

0 CURSE~
Syntax: cast curse <character>

Lowers the victim's hitroll and saving throw against spells by an eighth
of the caster's level, for twice the caster's level in ticks.  A cursed
character cannot RECALL.  REMOVE CURSE lifts it.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:21  Cleric:19  Thief:25  Warrior:23  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:22

See also: BLESS, REMOVE CURSE, MALADICTIONS
~

0 'DEMONFIRE'~
Syntax: cast demonfire <victim>

Calls the fires of hell on one victim: unholy damage of the caster's
level in ten-sided dice, halved by a saving throw.

  - Only an evil player can aim it.  If you are not evil, the demons
    turn on you and you take the damage yourself.
  - Every cast moves your alignment 50 toward the dark.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:36  Cleric:34  Thief:39  Warrior:37  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISPEL EVIL, DISPEL GOOD, ALIGNMENT, ATTACK
~

0 'DETECT EVIL'~
Syntax: cast 'detect evil'

Lets you see evil characters by a red aura.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:10  Thief:13  Warrior:13  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT GOOD, KNOW ALIGNMENT, DETECTION
~

0 'DETECT GOOD'~
Syntax: cast 'detect good'

Lets you see good characters by a silver aura.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:10  Thief:13  Warrior:13  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT EVIL, KNOW ALIGNMENT, DETECTION
~

0 'DETECT HIDDEN'~
Syntax: cast 'detect hidden'

Lets you see characters who are hiding.  It does not reveal STEALTH or
SHADOWMELD.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:9  Cleric:9  Thief:14  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT INVIS, FAERIE FOG, DETECTION
~

0 'DETECT INVIS'~
Syntax: cast 'detect invis'

Lets you see invisible characters and objects.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:7  Thief:11  Warrior:11  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT HIDDEN, INVIS
~

0 'DETECT MAGIC'~
Syntax: cast 'detect magic'

Lets you see which objects are magical.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:2  Cleric:2  Thief:5  Warrior:5  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: IDENTIFY, DETECT INVIS, DETECTION
~

0 'DETECT POISON'~
Syntax: cast 'detect poison' <object>

Tells you whether food or drink is poisoned.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:12  Cleric:7  Thief:9  Warrior:15  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CURE POISON, DETECT MAGIC
~

0 'DETECT TRAPS'~
Syntax: cast 'detect traps'

Reveals any trap in the room, on an object or on a door.  Mages and
clerics, from level 11.

See also: SEARCH, DETECT HIDDEN, DETECTION
~

0 'DISPEL EVIL'~
Syntax: cast 'dispel evil' <victim>

Holy damage against an evil victim, halved by a saving throw.  Good
victims are protected and neutral ones unaffected.  An evil player who
casts it strikes themselves.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:23  Cleric:23  Thief:29  Warrior:29  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISPEL GOOD, ALIGNMENT, ATTACK
~

0 'DISPEL GOOD'~
Syntax: cast 'dispel good' <victim>

Unholy damage against a good victim, halved by a saving throw.  Evil
victims are protected and neutral ones unaffected.  A good player who
casts it strikes themselves.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:23  Cleric:23  Thief:29  Warrior:29  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISPEL EVIL, ALIGNMENT, ATTACK
~

0 'DISPEL MAGIC' CANCELLATION 'NEUTRALITY FIELD'~
Syntax: cast 'dispel magic' <character>
        cast cancellation <character>
        cast 'neutrality field'

Remove magical effects, good and bad alike.  The higher an effect's
level, the harder; permanent effects (a mobile's own sanctuary) are
hardest.  Poison and plague cannot be dispelled.

  DISPEL MAGIC      one target; less reliable, and an attack
  CANCELLATION      allies only; more reliable, not an attack.  A player
                    must have NOSUMMON off to be cancelled.
  NEUTRALITY FIELD  dispel magic on everybody in the room; necromancers
                    only, from level 40

For dispel magic, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:16  Cleric:18  Thief:20  Warrior:22  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For cancellation, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:18  Cleric:16  Thief:22  Warrior:20  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:20

See also: REMOVE CURSE, NOSUMMON, PROTECTIVE
~

0 EARTHQUAKE~
Syntax: cast earthquake

Damages everybody in the room you could attack.  Others not yet fighting
may turn on you.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:14  Cleric:14  Thief:17  Warrior:17  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: ATTACK, ARCANE STUDIES, HARMFUL
~

0 'ELECTRIC SPELLS' 'SHOCKING GRASP' 'LIGHTNING BOLT' 'CHAIN LIGHTNING'
'CALL LIGHTNING'~
Syntax: cast 'shocking grasp'   <victim>
        cast 'lightning bolt'   <victim>
        cast 'chain lightning'  <victim>
        cast 'call lightning'

Lightning damage spells; the higher-level ones hurt more.

  LIGHTNING BOLT   a ten-sided die per caster level for a mage; other
                   classes roll half the dice
  CHAIN LIGHTNING  jumps from victim to victim in the room, starting
                   with the one named, and may strike the caster.  Full
                   mages, from level 38.
  CALL LIGHTNING   outdoors in bad weather only

For shocking grasp, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:12  Thief:13  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For lightning bolt, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:17  Cleric:19  Thief:21  Warrior:21  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For call lightning, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:26  Cleric:26  Thief:30  Warrior:30  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FIRE SPELLS, COLD SPELLS, WEATHERSPELLS
~

0 EMBALM~
Syntax: cast embalm <corpse or body part>

Makes a corpse or body part last longer before it decays, up to a limit;
past it the spell fails.  Necromancers only, from level 7.

See also: ANIMATE PARTS, BUTCHER, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 'ENCHANT ARMOR'~
Syntax: cast 'enchant armor' <armor>

Improves a piece of armour you carry (not wear) by 1 point of armour
class, or by 2 and a glow, and raises its level by one.

  - The more it is already enchanted, the likelier it fails.  A failure
    may do nothing, damage it badly, or make it explode.
  - Full mages, from level 30 (ENCHANTMENT group).

See also: ENCHANT WEAPON, ENCHANT ITEM, ENCHANTMENT
~

0 'ENCHANT WEAPON'~
Syntax: cast 'enchant weapon' <weapon>

Improves a weapon you carry (not wield): +1 hitroll and damroll, or +2
and a glow, and raises its level by one.

  - Each enchantment and bonus already on it makes failure likelier; half
    of all failures make it explode.
  - An enchanted weapon can no longer be dual wielded.
  - Full mages, from level 40 (ENCHANTMENT group).

See also: ENCHANT ARMOR, ENCHANT ITEM, SECONDARY
~

0 'ENCHANT ITEM'~
Syntax: cast 'enchant item' <object>

Lays a random change on one attribute of a weapon, armour, light, wand
or staff you carry -- most often for the worse ("shimmers with a black
aura").  A success marks it enchanted and raises its level by one.

  - Costs 100 mana.  Each affect already on it makes failure likelier: a
    failure may do nothing, or the object may evaporate or explode.  An
    object with no affects never fails.
  - Full mages, from level 16 (ENCHANTMENT group).

See also: ENCHANT ARMOR, ENCHANT WEAPON, LORE
~

0 'ENERGY DRAIN' 'VAMPIRIC TOUCH'~
Syntax: cast 'energy drain'   <victim>
        cast 'vampiric touch' <victim>

ENERGY DRAIN saps the victim's experience, mana and movement.

VAMPIRIC TOUCH drains life: you gain half of the hit points the touch
really takes.  A victim it cannot hurt gives nothing.  Necromancers only,
from level 15.

For energy drain, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:35  Cleric:36  Thief:40  Warrior:40  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:28

See also: MALADICTIONS, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 'EVIL EYE'~
Syntax: cast 'evil eye' <victim>

Turns your gaze into a weapon against one victim.  Necromancers only,
from level 19.

See also: BLINDNESS, ENERGY DRAIN, NECROMANCER
~

0 'FAERIE FIRE'~
Syntax: cast 'faerie fire' <victim>

Outlines the victim in pink light, worsening their armour class by 10
plus the caster's level, for 3 plus an eighth of the caster's level in
ticks.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:5  Cleric:6  Thief:8  Warrior:8  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FAERIE FOG, WEATHERSPELLS
~

0 'FAERIE FOG'~
Syntax: cast 'faerie fog'

Reveals invisible, hidden, sneaking and stealthed characters in the room.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:14  Cleric:16  Thief:20  Warrior:18  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FAERIE FIRE, DETECT HIDDEN, WEATHERSPELLS
~

0 'FIRE SPELLS' 'BURNING HANDS' 'FIREBALL' 'METEOR SWARM' 'FLAMESTRIKE'~
Syntax: cast 'burning hands' <victim>
        cast fireball        <victim>
        cast 'meteor swarm'
        cast flamestrike     <victim>

Fire damage spells; the higher-level ones hurt more.

  FLAMESTRIKE   a nine-sided die per caster level for a cleric; other
                classes roll half the dice
  METEOR SWARM  four balls of fire among your foes; several may strike
                one.  Full mages, from level 46.

For burning hands, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:7  Cleric:8  Thief:9  Warrior:10  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For fireball, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:22  Cleric:26  Thief:28  Warrior:30  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For flamestrike, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:23  Cleric:20  Thief:27  Warrior:25  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: COLD SPELLS, ELECTRIC SPELLS, ELEMENTAL
~

0 FIRESHIELD FROSTSHIELD 'DEATHSHROUD' 'DEATH SHROUD' 'FIRE SHIELD' 'FROST SHIELD'~
Syntax: cast 'fire shield'
        cast 'frost shield'
        cast 'death shroud'

Wrap you in a shield that hurts anybody who strikes you.

  - Fire shield: fire attacks against you do more damage.  Frost shield:
    cold attacks do.
  - Death shroud is hot or cold at random.
  - Fire and frost shield: full mages, from level 19.  Death shroud:
    necromancers, from level 22.

See also: ARMOR, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 FLY~
Syntax: cast fly <character>

Lets the target fly: over water, into the sky, and without falling.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:10  Cleric:11  Thief:12  Warrior:13  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:13

See also: LEVITATE, PASS DOOR, TRANSPORT
~

0 'FORCE SWORD'~
Syntax: cast 'force sword'

Conjures a magical sword at your side that attacks each round you do.
You show as (Guarded).  Full mages from level 32, necromancers from 34.

See also: POWER GLOVES, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 FRENZY~
Syntax: cast frenzy <character>

Fills the target with holy wrath: better hitroll and damroll, worse
armour class.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:N/A  Cleric:27  Thief:N/A  Warrior:N/A  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: HASTE, BERSERK, BENEDICTIONS
~

0 GATE 'EARTH TRAVEL'~
Syntax: cast gate <character>
        cast 'earth travel' <character>

Carries you to another character.

  - A player target must have NOSUMMON off.
  - The target may be no more than four levels above you, not an
    immortal, and not in a no-recall room or jail, nor anywhere you
    could not walk into: a full private room, a guild hall or guarded
    room closed to you, a Hyrule dungeon you have not earned.
  - With several of one name it goes to the first you could reach;
    2.kitten means the second.
  - Earth travel: necromancers only, from level 25.

For gate, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:20  Cleric:19  Thief:22  Warrior:24  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: PORTAL, SUMMON, TRANSPORT
~

0 'GIANT STRENGTH'~
Syntax: cast 'giant strength' <character>

Raises the target's strength.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:11  Cleric:13  Thief:14  Warrior:15  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: WEAKEN, HASTE, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 HASTE~
Syntax: cast haste <character>

Speeds the target up: an extra attack each round and a little more DEX,
for a third of the caster's level in ticks.  Cast on somebody slowed, it
lifts SLOW instead.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:21  Cleric:25  Thief:27  Warrior:29  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: SLOW, FRENZY, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 'DIVINE INTERVENTION'~
Syntax: cast 'divine intervention'

Restores the hit points and movement of everybody in your group in the
room, you included, to full -- and spends all your mana.  You need at
least 130 mana, and everybody it touches ends up resting.  Full clerics,
from level 43.

See also: HEALSPELL, HOLY WORD, HEALING
~

0 EMPOWER TITANIC 'EMPOWER SPELL' 'TITANIC SPELL'~
EMPOWER and TITANIC are bundles of power nobody can learn to cast.
Hermie hands out EMPOWER free when she is about (BUFF EMPOWER); the
rarest crafted potions and scrolls carry either.

EMPOWER lays sanctuary, haste, fly, pass door, protection evil, a fire
shield, divine protection and giant strength, with +15 INT, WIS and CON,
+11 DEX, +20 hitroll and damroll, -100 armour class, and adds half again
to the experience you earn.

TITANIC makes your maximum hit points, mana and movement five times what
they were, fills them, and adds half again to the experience you earn.
When it ends your pools fall back.

  - A crafted one lasts half its maker's level in ticks, at most 30, and
    is refused to anybody below the maker's level.
  - Players only; refused while you already carry it.
  - They are not the quest master's Potion of Power and Potion of the
    Giant, which hold ordinary spells.

See also: HERMIE, CONCOCT, SCRIBE, DIVINE PROTECTION
~

0 'DIVINE PROTECTION'~
Divine protection cannot be learned.  It comes from EMPOWER (Hermie) and
a few potions and staves.  For six ticks:

  - damage that is not mental is cut by a quarter (less with sanctuary);
  - blows against you are often answered with a counter-strike;
  - once, a blow that would kill you leaves you at three quarters of your
    hit points, mana and movement instead, and the protection ends.

It cannot be laid twice.  CANCELLATION removes it; DISPEL MAGIC does not.

See also: EMPOWER, SANCTUARY, CANCELLATION
~

0 HAVEN 'ROPE TRICK'~
Syntax: cast 'rope trick'
        cast haven

Opens a pocket dimension, joined to nothing, to rest in until the spell
ends.  Rope trick takes only you; haven takes your whole group and lasts
longer.  The duration varies each cast.

  - Rope trick: full mages and full clerics from level 31, necromancers
    from 33.
  - Haven: full mages and full clerics from level 44, necromancers from
    51.

See also: MAZE, PROTECTIVE, TRANSPORT
~

0 'HEAT METAL'~
Syntax: cast 'heat metal' <victim>

Heats the victim's metal armour and weapons, burning them; a piece they
cannot take off burns more.  Full mages from level 17, full clerics from
19.

See also: FIRE SPELLS, PYROTECHNICS, ATTACK
~

0 'HOLY WORD'~
Syntax: cast 'holy word'

A word of divine power to the whole room.  Those who share your
alignment are blessed and frenzied; those of the opposite side (or every
other side, if you are neutral) are cursed and struck.  It leaves you
with no movement and half your hit points.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:35  Cleric:32  Thief:37  Warrior:39  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DISPEL EVIL, DIVINE INTERVENTION, BENEDICTIONS
~

0 IDENTIFY~
Syntax: cast identify <object>

Tells you exactly what an object is and does.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:15  Cleric:16  Thief:18  Warrior:20  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: LORE, DETECT MAGIC, DETECTION
~

0 INFRAVISION~
Syntax: cast infravision <character>

Lets the target see in the dark.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:8  Cleric:10  Thief:13  Warrior:16  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:9

Any mage, cleric, thief or warrior can buy it, whatever their guild, from
their class guildmaster in Dresden as the NIGHT VISION group.

See also: DETECT HIDDEN, CONTINUAL LIGHT, NIGHT VISION
~

0 INVIS INVISSPELL 'MASS INVIS'~
Syntax: cast invis <character>
        cast 'mass invis'

INVIS makes the target invisible until they attack.  MASS INVIS makes
your whole group invisible, you included; full mages, from level 22.

For invis, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:5  Cleric:7  Thief:9  Warrior:11  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT INVIS, FAERIE FOG, BEGUILING
~

0 'KNOW ALIGNMENT'~
Syntax: cast 'know alignment' <character>

Tells you the target's alignment.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:12  Cleric:9  Thief:20  Warrior:15  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: DETECT EVIL, DETECT GOOD, ALIGNMENT
~

0 'LIGHT SPELLS' 'MOONBEAM' 'SUNRAY'~
Syntax: cast moonbeam <victim>
        cast sunray   <victim>

Light damage spells that work only at their time of day: MOONBEAM at
night, SUNRAY by day.  Moonbeam: necromancers only, from level 27.

For sunray, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:31  Cleric:31  Thief:46  Warrior:49  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CONTINUAL LIGHT, ELEMENTAL, HARMFUL
~

0 'LOCATE OBJECT'~
Syntax: cast 'locate object' <name>

Shows where objects of that name are.  Some objects cannot be located.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:9  Cleric:13  Thief:15  Warrior:18  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: IDENTIFY, TELEKINESIS, DETECTION
~

0 'MANA CONVERT'~
Syntax: cast 'mana convert'

Turns your own vigour into mana: clerics pay in movement, others in hit
points.  Refused when your mana is within 15 of full.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:13  Cleric:12  Thief:16  Warrior:16  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:14

See also: REFRESH, MEDITATION, BENEDICTIONS
~

0 MAZE~
Syntax: cast maze <victim>

Leaves the victim lost: they may try to go north and wander off another
way.  Full mages, full clerics and necromancers, from level 38.

See also: HAVEN, TRAP THE SOUL, MALADICTIONS
~

0 'PASS DOOR'~
Syntax: cast 'pass door'

Lets you pass through closed doors.  A locked door in Hyrule still stops
you.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:24  Cleric:22  Thief:28  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:24

See also: FLY, TRANSPORT, GHOSTLY PRESENCE
~

0 PLAGUE~
Syntax: cast plague <victim>

Diseases the victim: weakened, hurt each tick, and able to spread it to
others near them.  CURE DISEASE ends it.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:23  Cleric:17  Thief:29  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:20

See also: CURE DISEASE, POISON, MALADICTIONS
~

0 POISON~
Syntax: cast poison <victim>

Poisons the victim, unless they save: -2 strength and slower healing for
the caster's level in ticks.  CURE POISON ends it.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:17  Cleric:12  Thief:13  Warrior:21  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:20

See also: CURE POISON, DETECT POISON, PLAGUE
~

0 'PROTECTION EVIL' SANCTUARY 'MASS SANCTUARY'~
Syntax: cast 'protection evil'
        cast sanctuary <character>
        cast 'mass sanctuary'

The PROTECTION EVIL spell reduces the damage taken from evil attackers by
a quarter.  The SANCTUARY spell reduces the damage taken from every attack
by one half.  MASS SANCTUARY lays sanctuary on your whole group (full
clerics, from level 35).  They combine.

For protection evil, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:11  Cleric:9  Thief:13  Warrior:12  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

For sanctuary, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:33  Cleric:21  Thief:45  Warrior:40  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:37

See also: ARMOR, BLESS, PROTECTIVE
~

0 'PORTAL'~
Syntax: cast portal <character>
        look in portal
        enter portal

Opens a portal beside you to another character, for your group to step
through.  It closes after a time or after a number of people, both set
by your level.

  - It may be opened out of a no-recall room, never to a target standing
    in one; never into or out of a jail.
  - LOOK IN PORTAL shows the far side; ENTER PORTAL goes through.
  - Full mages from level 29, full clerics from 30.

See also: GATE, TELEPORT, RECALL, TRANSPORT
~

0 'POWER GLOVES'~
Syntax: cast 'power gloves'

Wraps your hands -- and any weapon you wield -- in an aura that adds to
the damage you do.  Full mages, from level 25.

See also: FORCE SWORD, GIANT STRENGTH, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 'RAISE DEAD'~
Syntax: cast 'raise dead' <corpse>

Brings a dead player back to you, without asking them, and returns each
item from their corpse they can carry; anything too heavy falls to the
ground beside them.  The corpse is used up.

  - Fails if the player is offline, has NOSUMMON on, or stands somewhere
    a summons cannot reach.
  - Nothing happens until the player's own file holds what was returned:
    if that cannot be written, the corpse and player stay as they were.
  - Full clerics from level 31, necromancers from 29.

See also: RESURRECTION, DEATH, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 RESURRECTION ACCEPT DECLINE~
Syntax: cast resurrection <corpse>
        accept
        decline

Offers a fallen player their own body back.  Cast it over their corpse;
the owner is asked wherever they are, and nothing happens until they
answer.  ACCEPT brings them to the corpse at one hit point with
everything it held, coin into the purse.  DECLINE, or two minutes'
silence, lets the call fade.

  - Members of the cleric guild only, whatever their class (it comes with
    the guild).  Qualo the healer trains it.
  - The dead cannot accept from a jail, a fight, or a room they could not
    RECALL out of, nor rise where they may not go; the call waits.
  - The corpse is used up.  Coin the purse cannot take falls beside it.

The minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:45  Cleric:40  Thief:50  Warrior:50  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: RAISE DEAD, DEATH, HEALING
~

0 REFRESH~
Syntax: cast refresh <character>

Restores movement.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:6  Cleric:4  Thief:8  Warrior:7  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: MANA CONVERT, AID, CREATION
~
0 'REMOVE ALIGN'~
Syntax: recite <scroll> <object>

Lifts an object's anti-good, anti-evil and anti-neutral restrictions --
unless it destroys the object instead.  The lower the scroll's level,
the likelier that is: four times in ten at level 20, once in ten at
level 50.  Nobody can learn it; it comes only on scribed scrolls.

See also: SCRIBE, RECITE, ALIGNMENT
~
0 'REMOVE CURSE'~
Syntax: cast 'remove curse' <character>

Removes a curse from a character, and may lift one from a cursed object
they hold.  Hyrule's bound items are not touched.

  - A player on NOSUMMON (the default) keeps their gear closed to it, from
    anybody, healers included: type NOSUMMON to open it first.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:20  Cleric:18  Thief:24  Warrior:22  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:20

See also: CURSE, NOSUMMON, CURATIVE
~

0 'RESTORE MANA'~
Nobody can learn restore mana.  It comes in potions and on staves, and a
few crafted potions carry it.  It gives back 5d10 mana, never past your
maximum.  Hermie fills your mana outright: BUFF MANA.

See also: BREW, CONCOCT, HERMIE, MEDITATION
~

0 'SKELETAL HANDS'~
Syntax: cast 'skeletal hands' <victim>

Skeletal hands claw up from the ground at the victim.  Necromancers
only, from level 13.

See also: ANIMATE PARTS, LIFE-UNDEATH, HARMFUL
~

0 SLEEPSPELL~
Syntax: cast sleep <victim>

Puts the victim to sleep until the spell ends or something wakes them.
Typing SLEEP without CAST puts you to sleep; see HELP SLEEP.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:12  Cleric:11  Thief:12  Warrior:14  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: CHARM PERSON, BEGUILING, MALADICTIONS
~

0 SLOW~
Syntax: cast slow <victim>

Slows the victim: fewer attacks and worse dodging.  Cast on somebody
hasted it removes the haste instead (a worn item's haste stays).

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:21  Cleric:29  Thief:26  Warrior:29  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: HASTE, ENHANCEMENT
~

0 'SPIRITUAL HAMMER'~
Syntax: cast 'spiritual hammer' <victim>

Throws a mystical hammer at the victim.  You must carry a weapon that
strikes like a hammer; the spell uses it up.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:21  Cleric:15  Thief:26  Warrior:29  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FORCE SWORD, HARMFUL
~

62 'STINKING CLOUD'~
Syntax: cast 'stinking cloud'

Fills the room with poisonous fumes for a short time: everybody else in
it is poisoned, takes damage and loses hitroll while they stay.  Staff
only.
~

0 SUMMON~
Syntax: cast summon <character>

Opens a short-lived portal beside the target that leads to you; they
choose whether to ENTER it.

  - The target must be below your level plus five, not fighting, not an
    aggressive or summon-proof mobile, and not a player on NOSUMMON.  A
    mobile may also resist.
  - Not to or from a jail or no-recall room, nor to a safe, private or
    solitary one.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:24  Cleric:12  Thief:29  Warrior:26  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: GATE, PORTAL, NOSUMMON
~

0 TELEPORT TELEPORTSPELL~
Syntax: cast teleport [character]

Sends somebody to a random location in the world -- a risk, since it is
a dangerous world.  With no target (or SELF) it moves you.  On anybody else
it is an attack: they get a saving throw and may fight back.

  - Fails from a no-recall room or jail, and on somebody fighting.
  - Never lands in a private, no-recall, jail, death trap or
    no-teleport room.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:13  Cleric:22  Thief:25  Warrior:36  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: WORD OF RECALL, RECALL, PORTAL
~

0 TENTACLES~
Syntax: cast tentacles

Massive tentacles rise from the ground and strike everybody in the room
you could attack.  Necromancers only, from level 42.

See also: SKELETAL HANDS, LIFE-UNDEATH, HARMFUL
~

0 'TRAP THE SOUL'~
Syntax: cast 'trap the soul' <victim>

Sucks a mobile into an empty soul container you carry; it stays there
until you open the container.  Players, Hyrule's creatures and protected
mobiles cannot be trapped.  Necromancers only, from level 51.

See also: MAZE, ANIMATE PARTS, LIFE-UNDEATH
~

0 VENTRILOQUATE~
Syntax: cast ventriloquate <speaker> <message>

Throws your voice so somebody or something in the room seems to say your
message; those who save know it was a trick.  No class can learn it.
~

62 WATERFALL~
Syntax: cast waterfall

This spell is inactive.
~

0 'WATER SPELLS' 'WATER BURST' 'GEYSER'~
Syntax: cast 'water burst' <victim>
        cast geyser        <victim>

Water damage spells that need water from a container you carry.
Water burst consumes 20 units and Geyser consumes 45 units; the
container and the rest of its water are kept.  Geyser: full mages and
full clerics, from level 43.

For water burst, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:19  Cleric:19  Thief:24  Warrior:24  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:N/A

See also: FIRE SPELLS, COLD SPELLS, ELEMENTAL
~

0 WEAKEN~
Syntax: cast weaken <victim>

Lowers the victim's strength, more for a higher-level caster.

Minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:11  Cleric:14  Thief:16  Warrior:17  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:18

See also: GIANT STRENGTH, CURSE, MALADICTIONS
~

0 'WIND SPELLS' 'DUST DEVIL' 'VORTEX'~
Syntax: cast 'dust devil' <victim>
        cast vortex       <victim>

Wind damage spells.  Vortex hurts more than dust devil.

For dust devil, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:15  Cleric:17  Thief:21  Warrior:21  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:19

For vortex, minimum level depends on your primary class and is:
Mage:40  Cleric:42  Thief:48  Warrior:48  Monk:N/A  Necromancer:44

See also: ELECTRIC SPELLS, ELEMENTAL, HARMFUL
~

0 'DOMINION SHIELD' 'BLOODY AURA' DSHIELD BAURA~
Wards some monsters raise in a fight.  No character can learn them.

  BLOODY AURA      turns every spell aside for a minute or two; weapons
                   still work, so close in and hit it
  DOMINION SHIELD  turns everything aside, weapon and spell alike, for
                   about a minute; raised only when the creature is badly
                   hurt.  Hold your ground and keep your healing up.

Both announce themselves rising and fading: if a creature has stopped
taking damage, read the last few lines.

See also: SANCTUARY, CONSIDER
~

0 'WORD OF RECALL'~
Syntax: cast 'word of recall'

Prays you home to the Temple.  Unlike the RECALL skill:

  - it always goes to the Temple, whatever recall point you have set;
  - a curse does not stop it.

A scroll or potion of recall carries this spell.  A no-recall room or a
jail still stops it.  Full clerics, from level 28.

See also: RECALL, TELEPORT, PORTAL
~

0 'DRACONIAN SPELLS' 'ACID BREATH' 'FIRE BREATH' 'FROST BREATH' 'GAS BREATH'
'LIGHTNING BREATH'~
Syntax: cast 'acid breath'      <victim>
        cast 'fire breath'      <victim>
        cast 'frost breath'     <victim>
        cast 'gas breath'
        cast 'lightning breath' <victim>

Dragon breath.  Acid, fire, frost and lightning hit one victim; gas hits
every player in the room.  Fire and frost can break objects, and acid
can damage armour.

Full mages only (DRACONIAN group): frost breath 34, lightning breath 36,
fire breath 39, acid breath 42, gas breath 44.

See also: FIRE SPELLS, COLD SPELLS, DRACONIAN
~

0 $~
